TKINT 

You spend your nights 
As kindling for a distant dawn,
Feeding the dark with 
Hours no one will remember. 
You sing to deaf ears. 
You dance for blind eyes. 
You are alone. 
You have always been alone. 
But that's okay because 
We feel alone too. 

AML

We are dwindling fires, 
Each convinced 
That the light is ours to keep. 
So take your embers, 
And call them company. 
They will not warm you 
But they will answer 
Your every call 
And they will keep you 
On this road 
That you have reaped, 
That you will sow. 
